<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 8 August, from 870 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">870</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Meerssen partitions Lotharingia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles the Bald and Louis the German divided the lands of their late nephew Lothair II between West and East Francia. The partition helped shape the later frontier between France and Germany.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1576</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Foundation stone is laid for Tycho Brahe's Uraniborg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Work began on Tycho Brahe's observatory on the island of Hven, granted to him by Frederick II of Denmark. Its precise naked-eye observations later allowed Kepler to derive his laws of planetary motion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1918</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied attack at Amiens breaks the German line</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British, Australian, Canadian and French troops, with hundreds of tanks, broke through near Amiens. Ludendorff called it the 'black day of the German army'; the Hundred Days Offensive had begun.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1945</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union declares war on Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Moscow declared war on Japan and, within hours, launched a massive invasion of Manchuria. Coming between the atomic bombings, it helped persuade Japan's leaders to surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1974</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard Nixon announces his resignation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a televised address, Richard Nixon said he would resign the presidency at noon the next day. Released tapes had proved his role in the Watergate cover-up, leaving him facing certain impeachment.</p></li></ol>
